{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "02821",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 1.34,
      "end_seconds": 7.92,
      "duration_seconds": 6.58,
      "text": "Right, doctor, hi, where would you like me to to put my coat?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 9.03,
      "end_seconds": 13.48,
      "duration_seconds": 4.45,
      "text": "You're alright, take a seat. What can I do for you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 14.65,
      "end_seconds": 18.6,
      "duration_seconds": 3.95,
      "text": "I'm here because of breathlessness building over weeks"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 19.9,
      "end_seconds": 22.69,
      "duration_seconds": 2.79,
      "text": "Has this been going on for long?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 24.39,
      "end_seconds": 29.02,
      "duration_seconds": 4.63,
      "text": "Um, I've had it for about a month."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 30.84,
      "end_seconds": 39.4,
      "duration_seconds": 8.56,
      "text": "Alright, can you describe it a bit more for me? How strong it is, what the pattern is, what helps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 40.86,
      "end_seconds": 56.92,
      "duration_seconds": 16.06,
      "text": "It's every other day. Moderate, really. I've had a dull ache on one side of the chest too, you know, for three days. I've also had a dry cough, since yesterday."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 57.47,
      "end_seconds": 64.63,
      "duration_seconds": 7.16,
      "text": "hm, okay. Any night sweats, fever, leg swelling or coughing up blood at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 66.03,
      "end_seconds": 72.49,
      "duration_seconds": 6.46,
      "text": "No night sweats, fever, leg swelling or coughing up blood, none of it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 73.03,
      "end_seconds": 75.03,
      "duration_seconds": 2.0,
      "text": "Is your mobility otherwise okay?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 76.57,
      "end_seconds": 78.15,
      "duration_seconds": 1.58,
      "text": "nothing else aches"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 78.98,
      "end_seconds": 80.95,
      "duration_seconds": 1.97,
      "text": "So, neurologically, anything strange?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 82.11,
      "end_seconds": 84.14,
      "duration_seconds": 2.03,
      "text": "no, that's all normal"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 86.13,
      "end_seconds": 91.32,
      "duration_seconds": 5.19,
      "text": "So, any allergies to tablets, food or anything in the environment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 92.6,
      "end_seconds": 94.63,
      "duration_seconds": 2.03,
      "text": "No allergies at all."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 95.26,
      "end_seconds": 99.88,
      "duration_seconds": 4.62,
      "text": "What about your parents, brothers or sisters, any conditions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 101.57,
      "end_seconds": 103.44,
      "duration_seconds": 1.87,
      "text": "My brother has epilepsy."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 122.42,
      "end_seconds": 126.05,
      "duration_seconds": 3.63,
      "text": "any health conditions I should have on record?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 129.75,
      "end_seconds": 132.78,
      "duration_seconds": 3.03,
      "text": "An underactive thyroid, for two years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 137.27,
      "end_seconds": 138.33,
      "duration_seconds": 1.06,
      "text": "Hm, okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 139.8,
      "end_seconds": 140.85,
      "duration_seconds": 1.05,
      "text": "Yes, gout."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 146.17,
      "end_seconds": 151.49,
      "duration_seconds": 5.32,
      "text": "okay, I can see an underactive thyroid in your file as well"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 168.74,
      "end_seconds": 171.96,
      "duration_seconds": 3.22,
      "text": "Okay, have you been to theatre before?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 173.3,
      "end_seconds": 179.68,
      "duration_seconds": 6.38,
      "text": "Just a cataract operation in my left eye, about a year ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 180.76,
      "end_seconds": 184.56,
      "duration_seconds": 3.8,
      "text": "Do you take any prescribed or over-the-counter medicines?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 186.02,
      "end_seconds": 200.24,
      "duration_seconds": 14.22,
      "text": "Let me think, I'm on Thyronorm, 50 micrograms, every morning. It's a relief to finally sit down and talk about it. It's allopurinol, 100 milligrams, once a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 201.97,
      "end_seconds": 203.37,
      "duration_seconds": 1.4,
      "text": "are you active?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 205.05,
      "end_seconds": 208.36,
      "duration_seconds": 3.31,
      "text": "I walk the dog every morning."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 209.47,
      "end_seconds": 212.29,
      "duration_seconds": 2.82,
      "text": "Do you follow any particular diet?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 213.2,
      "end_seconds": 216.73,
      "duration_seconds": 3.53,
      "text": "I'm vegetarian and have been for years"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 219.9,
      "end_seconds": 221.58,
      "duration_seconds": 1.68,
      "text": "who lives with you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 226.68,
      "end_seconds": 229.26,
      "duration_seconds": 2.58,
      "text": "My partner and our baby."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 231.28,
      "end_seconds": 236.74,
      "duration_seconds": 5.46,
      "text": "Alright, can I check a few measurements before we carry on?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 244.68,
      "end_seconds": 247.24,
      "duration_seconds": 2.56,
      "text": "keep your arm relaxed for me.."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 262.14,
      "end_seconds": 275.35,
      "duration_seconds": 13.21,
      "text": "Okay: SpO2 89 percent on room air, pulse is 85 beats a minute, temperature is 37.1 degrees. And blood pressure 140 over 76, respiratory rate 26."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 277.22,
      "end_seconds": 281.27,
      "duration_seconds": 4.05,
      "text": "alright, over here please and I'll take a look"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 283.08,
      "end_seconds": 285.05,
      "duration_seconds": 1.97,
      "text": "Alright, does that hurt?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 302.14,
      "end_seconds": 307.25,
      "duration_seconds": 5.11,
      "text": "There is dullness to percussion and reduced breath sounds at the right base."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 309.56,
      "end_seconds": 312.41,
      "duration_seconds": 2.85,
      "text": "Thank you, you can get dressed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 323.75,
      "end_seconds": 330.05,
      "duration_seconds": 6.3,
      "text": "Having listened and examined, it points towards a pleural effusion needing a cause."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 330.81,
      "end_seconds": 333.16,
      "duration_seconds": 2.35,
      "text": "Is it dangerous, doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 334.81,
      "end_seconds": 357.49,
      "duration_seconds": 22.68,
      "text": "It's reasonable to be concerned, but right now a pleural effusion needing a cause is my leading thought, not anything worse. I'd like to arrange a CT scan of the chest for pleural effusion. I'll request a chest X-ray, it'll help with breathlessness. I am arranging an urgent chest clinic review."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 358.02,
      "end_seconds": 371.27,
      "duration_seconds": 13.25,
      "text": "I see, go ahead. Please don't wait if the symptoms get worse. That's when to be seen urgently. Let's review you after the scan. That's everything on my side. Anything you're unsure about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 372.54,
      "end_seconds": 375.52,
      "duration_seconds": 2.98,
      "text": "Hmm, alright, thanks, take care."
    }
  ]
}